    "complete_transaction": {
      "_description": "GET /api/v1/transactions/2 - the complex nested object required by the assignment. A single response containing the transaction, its category (FK join), both participants (M:N junction resolved, with the role attribute from the junction), its tags (second M:N junction, carrying confidence and tagged_by from the relationship), the raw source message, and the ETL log entries for this record. Seven tables are represented in one object. This particular transaction was chosen because its receiver is a merchant till with no MSISDN: the participant shows a party_ref, a null-derived phone_number and has_msisdn=false, which is the party_ref design working rather than merely being described.",
      "data": {
        "transaction_id": 2,
        "reference": "TXN002",
        "category": {
          "category_id": 3,
          "code": "PAYMENT_MERCHANT",
          "name": "Merchant Payment",
